        "id": 2921717,
        "name": "Namdor",
        "username": "Namdor",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.eveonline.com/namdor/{size}/396179_2.png",
        "created_at": "2026-09-02T22:32:28.789Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I use AI quite a lot, and what I’m criticizing here isn’t the AI, but rather its unskilled, uncritical, and most of all <em>lazy</em> utilization.</p>\n<p>I’ve heard software developers complain that, of late, they just do QC for the AI, but uh… You can’t just <em>skip</em> the QC part, which is clearly what OP has done here.</p>\n<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://global.discourse-cdn.com/eveonline/original/4X/a/d/4/ad4bd4b15f5b00f43f3230f925807aedbaada125.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/oJ34hZ4xSkm8VzpB49CjfNO9Gzb.png?dl=1\" title=\"image\"><img src=\"https://global.discourse-cdn.com/eveonline/original/4X/a/d/4/ad4bd4b15f5b00f43f3230f925807aedbaada125.png\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"oJ34hZ4xSkm8VzpB49CjfNO9Gzb\" width=\"690\" height=\"410\" data-dominant-color=\"161D25\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">image</span><span class=\"informations\">698×415 18.9 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div></p>\n<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://global.discourse-cdn.com/eveonline/original/4X/9/1/f/91f564c906d00af18e655813b58d3b970116b829.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/kPcZbarkubDFa9xeZ7dXjt1he3f.jpeg?dl=1\" title=\"image\"><img src=\"https://global.discourse-cdn.com/eveonline/original/4X/9/1/f/91f564c906d00af18e655813b58d3b970116b829.jpeg\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"kPcZbarkubDFa9xeZ7dXjt1he3f\" width=\"617\" height=\"500\" data-dominant-color=\"1A1918\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">image</span><span class=\"informations\">640×518 69.3 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div></p>\n<p>It’s only wrong by <em>about</em> 20%, so I can see how it could be easily overlooked by a blind person who also never checked the output even a single time.</p>\n<p>Doing a little bit of napkin math here, it looks like this is probably calculating it as:</p>\n<p>JobFee = EIV * SCI * (1+surchage+tax)<br>\nFor an MTU in Jita that’s:</p>\n<p>5177367 * .1707 * 1.0425 = 921,337</p>\n<p>The correct calculation is actually:</p>\n<p>EIV * SCI + EIV * (surchage+tax):</p>\n<p>5177367 * .1707 + 5177367 * .0425 = 1,103,814</p>\n<p>Now, this is an easily fixed bug, but it’s also an extremely obvious one that anyone would catch either at a glance, if they’re very familiar with prices, or during even the most casual of testing.</p>\n<p>OP did not even queue a job to see if the values his calculator outputs matches the ingame values, he just called it good enough, slapped a Ko-Fi donation button on it, and shipped it.</p>\n<p>I would go on, but I am pretty sure that I have already given this app more <em>human</em> mindshare than anyone else on the planet.</p>",
